: ASM_ARCH=x86_64_nasm_gnu,x86_64_nasm_macho :
: BLOCK_TEST :
: RUN_ASM :

:/
Reduced from the initial 491/492 calls with unsuffixed index/depth literals.
Expected: the i32 argument receives zero, even though the function is generic.
cplc 4.0.4:1711.26, x86_64 Mach-O, -O0: exit 1 instead of 42.
The caller writes SIL, while the callee reads ESI. Seed RSI with 256 so stale
upper bits are deterministic. Explicit 0i32 avoids this defect.
/:
@[inline(never)]
function argument501<T>(T unused, i32 value) -> i32 { return value; }

start() {
    asm() { "mov rsi, 256" }
    if argument501<i8>(0i8, 0i32) != 0; { exit 1; }
    exit 42;
}

:/ OUTPUT
@exit_code=42
